# Env & secrets — never commit. Listed first and deliberately broad, because this
# repository is published on its own: the monorepo's ignore rules do not travel
# with a split, and a tree copied into a repo whose rules did not travel is how a
# live provider key gets one commit away from being public. `naive up` reads your
# keys from the shell (`{ from_env }` in naive.config.ts), so nothing here should
# ever hold one — these rules are what make "should" into "did not".
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.dev.vars*
!.dev.vars.example
*.pem
*.key

# deps
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/

# build output
dist/
build/
.vercel/
.wrangler/
*.tsbuildinfo

# Runtime state of the local JSON store (server/store.ts) — never committed.
data/

# misc
.DS_Store
*.log
coverage/
